   },
   {
    "id": 866735,
    "guid": "409AB7A0305B11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866734,
    "previous_guid": "2B7163B0305B11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare seeds</p>",
    "section_color": "#A492FF",
    "section_duration": 86400,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Incubate the seeds in MQ water in the dark at 4C at least overnight, but not longer than one week, to break the seed dormancy",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "3",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866736,
    "guid": "54BC86A0305B11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866735,
    "previous_guid": "409AB7A0305B11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Using the large and sturdy scissors - cut the yellow pipette tip so that you only keep the wider stud - as in the picture \n\n[pipette.jpg]](https://content.protocols.io/public/24ade3775508737138210a168177a0a1d3ca4b004ce7fb1ed98a69963474311a/bwhxg3kw.jpg)\nThe studed pipette tip - the bottom one is the desired cut of the pipette tip  \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "4",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866737,
    "guid": "3D561E80305C11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866736,
    "previous_guid": "54BC86A0305B11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Prepare Agar medium solution. Per 1 L use:\n\n2.2 g Murashi Skoog nutrients\n1 g MES buffer\nadjust pH with KOH to 5.8\n\nAfter adjusting pH add 10 g of Dashin Agar\n\nAutoclave the solution or melt the agar in the microwave.\n\nYou can store the nutrient agar solution on your benchtop, at room temperature, for about two weeks, or at 65 C cabinet for up to three days. Before using make sure that the solution is liquid by warming it up in the microwave ",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "5",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866738,
    "guid": "BFE371E0305C11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866737,
    "previous_guid": "3D561E80305C11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Put the pipette studs into a clean PCR plate and add liquid nutrient agar solution so that it covers the bottom part - wait for the solution to solidify. \n\nAfter the initial solidification of the media in the bottom part of the pipette tip - add more agar to fill the pipette tip\n\nTIP: Make sure that your media forms a meniscus rather than a &#34;bulb&#34; - this will make it easier to place tiny Arabidopsis seeds without them sliding to the side\n\n[PCR plate.jpg]](https://content.protocols.io/public/24ade3775508737138210a168177a0a1d3ca4b004ce7fb1ed98a69963474311a/bwhyg3kw.jpg)\npipette studs in the final stage of filling them with nutrient agar solution \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "6",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866739,
    "guid": "33AC40C0305D11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866738,
    "previous_guid": "BFE371E0305C11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Put the agar-filled pipette studs into the 1 ml tip box (they should be placed deeper into the box than in &#34;yellow tip box&#34;), fill the box using the liquid medium. Per 1L of liquid medium you need:\n\n2.2 g Murashi Skoog nutrients\n1 g MES buffer\nadjust pH with KOH to 5.8\n\nThe above solution does not have to be autoclaved - unless you have a specific reason to do so. ",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "7",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866740,
    "guid": "71F8E450305D11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866739,
    "previous_guid": "33AC40C0305D11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Using 1 ml pipette tip - drop the Arabidopsis seeds that underwent 24h cold treatment on top of the agar in the pipette studs. Place the pipette tip boxes in the growth chamber set at 18C, 12h light/dark cycle, 60% humidity for the seeds to germinate.\n\n[seeds in.jpg]](https://content.protocols.io/public/24ade3775508737138210a168177a0a1d3ca4b004ce7fb1ed98a69963474311a/bwhzg3kw.jpg)\n \n\nNOTE - it is important that the boxes are covered with the transparent lid - so the agar in the studs won&#39;t dry out\n\n[closed boxes.jpg]](https://content.protocols.io/public/24ade3775508737138210a168177a0a1d3ca4b004ce7fb1ed98a69963474311a/bwh2g3kw.jpg)\n \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "8",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866741,
    "guid": "E7070470305D11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866740,
    "previous_guid": "71F8E450305D11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Make sure to check on the level of liquid media every day and replace the media completely every 5-7 days\n\nFour days after placing the boxes into the growth room you should observe thegermination of your seeds. I would advise you to &#34;thin out&#34; the seedlings at this stage - so you have only one germinating seedling per agar stud\n\n[4 dag.jpg]](https://content.protocols.io/public/24ade3775508737138210a168177a0a1d3ca4b004ce7fb1ed98a69963474311a/bwh3g3kw.jpg)\nArabidopsis seedlings 4 days after germination \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "9",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866742,
    "guid": "383E0870305E11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866741,
    "previous_guid": "E7070470305D11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "The roots should grow out of the agar studs between one and two weeks after germination. The level of media is adjusted as not to cover the studs completely, but rather be just below the plate holding the pipette tip studs\n\n[1 week old seedling.jpg]](https://content.protocols.io/public/24ade3775508737138210a168177a0a1d3ca4b004ce7fb1ed98a69963474311a/bwh4g3kw.jpg)\nOne week old seedlings of Arabidopsis in pipette-tip hydroponics \n[2 weeks old seedling.jpg]](https://content.protocols.io/public/24ade3775508737138210a168177a0a1d3ca4b004ce7fb1ed98a69963474311a/bwh5g3kw.jpg)\ntwo weeks old seedlings of Arabidopsis \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "10",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866743,
    "guid": "8F91D660305E11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866742,
    "previous_guid": "383E0870305E11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "After two weeks of growth, the seedlings are transferred to larger hydroponics containers with 2L of solution per container \n[larger containers.jpg]](https://content.protocols.io/public/24ade3775508737138210a168177a0a1d3ca4b004ce7fb1ed98a69963474311a/bwh6g3kw.jpg)\nTwo weeks old seedlings transferred to the larger Ara-ponics containers \n\n\n\n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "11",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 866744,
    "guid": "1AFE20F0305F11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "previous_id": 866743,
    "previous_guid": "8F91D660305E11EAA00BC547A53CE423",
    "section": "<p>Prepare pipette studs</p>",
    "section_color": "#94EBFF",
    "section_duration": 3600,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "For RNA-seq analysis, we add 100 mM NaCl to the liquid nutrient solution (as described above), when replacing the medium at 3 weeks after germination and harvest the shoot and root tissue to separate tubes for RNA isolation. \n\nSUGGESTION: If you wish to treat your seedlings with salt stress, you could do it at earlier stage, as soon as the root will grow out of the agar stud",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 31494,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "0",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "12",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   }
